  "short_model": "BASgatewayLX ION6200",
  "model_slug": "basgatewaylx-schneider-ion6200",
  "aliases": [
    "ION6200",
    "PowerLogic ION6200"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Power and energy meter",
  "applies_to": "Schneider Electric PowerLogic ION6200 meters on Modbus, read by a BASgatewayLX.",
  "summary": "Gateway profile for the ION6200: 134 objects (129 AI, 5 AO), 22 polled by default. Polled inputs give phase and average voltages and currents, current demand, frequency, PF, kW totals and phases and kVAR/kVA demand; energy, peak demand and setup values are unpolled, and five unpolled outputs reset energy and demand or drive the two digital outputs.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Schneider_Electric_ION6200_a_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the maker's Modbus register document (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/ion6200%20registers.pdf).",
    "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
    "Only 22 of the 134 rows are flagged for polling in the profile; the rest are served only after you tick them in the gateway. Their descriptions say \"not polled by default\".",
    "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads.",
    "Some names appear more than once in the profile as published (kWh del; kWh rec; kVARh del...); they are kept as printed and told apart by instance."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Schneider_Electric_ION6200_a",
    "doc_number": "Schneider_Electric_ION6200_a_LX.csv",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/Schneider_Electric_ION6200.zip"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Map total kW, kWh delivered and average line-line voltage first. The listed objects are read-only.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "AI 31",
        "name": "kW total",
        "why": "Total kW"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 49",
        "name": "kWh del",
        "why": "kWh delivered"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 18",
        "name": "Vll avg",
        "why": "Average line-line voltage"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 22",
        "name": "I avg",
        "why": "Average current"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 27",
        "name": "PF sign total",
        "why": "Total power factor (signed)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 26",
        "name": "Frequency",
        "why": "Frequency"
      }
    ],
    "enable": null,
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "The BASgatewayLX presents each Modbus device as its own virtual BACnet device on BACnet IP; give it a unique device instance and Modbus address (serial) or IP address (Modbus TCP) when you add it with this profile.",
      "One BASgatewayLX handles up to 100 Modbus devices and 1000 polled points in total, so leave unneeded rows unpolled."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "kWh del appears twice (AI 49 with units, AI 81 without) as printed; check the register document for the scaling of each.",
      "Unpolled rows do not appear as BACnet objects until enabled in the gateway's device profile page."
    ]
  },
